  "summary": "This project connects two isolated Amazon VPCs in the ap-southeast-2 (Sydney) region using a VPC peering connection. A bastion host in the public subnet of VPC A is used to administer private instances in both VPCs.",

  "objectives": [
    "Create two isolated VPCs with non-overlapping CIDR blocks in ap-southeast-2.",
    "Establish a VPC peering connection between VPC A and VPC B.",
    "Configure route tables so the private subnets can reach each other over the peering connection.",
    "Restrict access with security groups and a bastion host.",
    "Verify connectivity with documented tests and screenshot evidence.",
    "Clean up all resources afterwards to avoid unnecessary charges."
  ],

  "architecture": {
    "description": "VPC A (10.10.0.0/16) contains a public subnet with a bastion host and a private subnet with the App-A instance. VPC B (10.20.0.0/16) contains a single private subnet with the App-B instance. A VPC peering connection links the two VPCs.\n\nPeering is not transitive and the CIDR blocks do not overlap. Each VPC route table needs an explicit route to the other VPC's CIDR block through the peering connection.",
